BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
70.8661417322834666 582.5199212598424765 Td
(Ischemic cerebral stroke initiates acute microglial polarization accompanied by catastrophic neurovascular breakdown.) Tj
T* (Despite recanalization therapies, post-ischemic secondary neuroinflammation remains therapeutically unaddressed.) Tj
T* (Here, we hypothesized that pharmacological inhibition of NLRP3 inflammasome priming via a novel small-molecule) Tj
T* (scaffold suppresses neurotoxic cytokines and salvages ischemic penumbral tissue.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.722 0.525 0.043 rg
70.8661417322834666 522.9923622047243725 Td
(Materials & Methods:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
70.8661417322834666 510.2364566929133503 Td
(Adult male Sprague-Dawley rats \(250–280 g, IAEC Approval # NIPER/IAEC/2026/04\) were subjected to 90-minute) Tj
T* (transient middle cerebral artery occlusion \(tMCAO\) followed by 24h reperfusion. Vehicle or Test Agent \(5, 10, 20 mg/kg) Tj
T* (i.v.\) was administered at reperfusion onset. Neurological deficit scoring \(mNSS\), TTC cerebral infarct planimetry,) Tj
T* (blood-brain barrier permeability \(Evans blue extravasation\), and immunofluorescence for Iba-1/GFAP were quantified.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.722 0.525 0.043 rg
70.8661417322834666 439.3703149606298552 Td
(Results & Discussion:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
70.8661417322834666 426.614409448818833 Td
(Test Agent \(10 mg/kg\) caused a 48.6% reduction in total cerebral infarct volume compared to vehicle-treated controls \(p) Tj
T* (< 0.001, one-way ANOVA with Dunnett's post-test\). Neurological deficit scores improved significantly within 24 hours) Tj
T* (\(mNSS 5.2 vs 11.8 in vehicle\). Western blotting of penumbral tissue confirmed downregulation of cleaved caspase-1 and) Tj
T* (mature IL-1beta without altering systemic hemodynamics.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.722 0.525 0.043 rg
70.8661417322834666 361.4175590551180335 Td
(Conclusions:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
70.8661417322834666 348.6616535433070112 Td
(The findings establish this novel pharmacophore as a potent, brain-penetrant neurovascular protective lead candidate) Tj
T* (capable of dampening neuroinflammation during the hyperacute reperfusion window.) Tj
